A||||11||ferg||drove the fiero for 1st time in a year||||14||
Z||000000||ferg||06-15-2001||10:18 AM||||For those who don't remember, my dad gave me the car as a graduation gift from college last year. He bought it in 1988 or 1989 for a toy. For the past 6 years it's been stored at my parents lake cottage (50 miles from my house), just waiting to be driven. As luck would have it, I was required to attend 6 weddings last summer. Since the car was that far from home and my tools, it sat. <P>My friend is getting new tires today at the Tire Rack and he's picking up my tires and shocks while he's there. <P>Me and my dad drove to the lake to get the car last night and with a jump the car fired right up. Got it on the highway and remembered real fast how badly I need an alignment.<P>I got it home with no problems and when I was putting it away for the night the parking brake light came on- read about it in the technical section.<P>The plan now is to get it emissions tested, change all the fluids, including the brake fluid, get my tires put on, replace shocks, get an alignment, and a few other things. Depending on the outcome of the brake problem in the other section, I think I'll have the car on the road by the middle of next week.<P>I can't wait- it's been too long||||reg||14
Z||000001||Cheever2||06-15-2001||12:56 PM||||I know how you feel.  Waited 19 months to get my GT back on the road.  Feels great.<BR>||||reg||6
